SUMMARY:Reporting from Contemporary Italy: Q&A with Jason Horowitz\, New Y
 ork Times Europe Correspondent
LOCATION:MIT\, 182 MEMORIAL DR\, Cambridge\, MA 02139
DESCRIPTION:Reporting from Contemporary Italy: Q&A with Jason Horowitz\, Ne
 w York Times Europe Correspondent As Rome Bureau Chief for the New York Ti
 mes for the last eight years\, Jason Horowitz reported from the front line
 s of Italy and the Mediterranean region. In his new book The Italian Job: 
 A Memoir of an American Reporter in Rome\, he shares an insider’s view o
 f politics and culture in Italy today\, including the rise of Giorgia Melo
 ni and the election of the first North American Pope.\nhttps://calendar.mi
 t.edu/event/reporting-from-contemporary-italy\nFrom Pushpin Boston: https:
 //pushpin.city/boston/
URL:https://calendar.mit.edu/event/reporting-from-contemporary-italy
END:VEVENT
