SUMMARY:Cities of Islamic Art: From Historical Visual Systems to the Format
 ion of Contemporary Islamic Art in North America
LOCATION:MIT\, 33 MASSACHUSETTS AVE\, Cambridge\, MA 02139
DESCRIPTION:This lecture uses Cities of Islamic Art\, Vol. 2 as both an obj
 ect and a methodology to examine Islamic art as a mobile system of visual 
 knowledge rather than a fixed historical style. Beginning with historical 
 surfaces from Isfahan\, Istanbul\, Damascus\, Cairo\, and Granada\, the ta
 lk traces how motifs migrate across ceramics\, tiles\, manuscripts\, and a
 rchitecture to form the fabric of visual culture and heritage known as “
 Islamic Art.”\nhttps://calendar.mit.edu/event/cities-of-islamic-art\nFro
 m Pushpin Boston: https://pushpin.city/boston/
URL:https://calendar.mit.edu/event/cities-of-islamic-art
END:VEVENT
